# SHA-pinned replay fixtures are byte artifacts; never rewrite line endings.
tests/fixtures/replay/** -text

# Shell scripts MUST check out LF, on every platform. `core.autocrlf=true` is
# the normal Windows setting and it gave `scripts/ci-local.sh` CRLF endings, so
# running the Linux CI leg under WSL against a Windows checkout died on line 1
# of real work:
#
#     scripts/ci-local.sh: line 50: set: pipefail: invalid option name
#     scripts/ci-local.sh: line 51: $'\r': command not found
#     scripts/ci-local.sh: line 61: syntax error near unexpected token `$'do\r''
#
# That is what made "just run ci-local before pushing" a Windows-only habit,
# and four POSIX-only failures shipped to CI behind it (see the sixth bullet in
# both ci-local scripts). `install.sh` has the same exposure for anyone who
# clones on Windows and runs it under WSL.
*.sh text eol=lf
